@LIC_ARCHIVE_DATA_ACKNOWLEDGEMENTS
Public archive data is not "licensed code", but each archive asks for an acknowledgement line and a data citation in any
paper or release that uses it. [MEMORY] wording; VERIFY exact text on the archive's own acknowledgement page before publishing.
  HST / JWST (MAST, STScI):  "Based on observations made with the NASA/ESA Hubble Space Telescope, obtained from the Mikulski Archive
        for Space Telescopes (MAST) at the Space Telescope Science Institute", plus programme IDs; cite the MAST DOI of the data used.
  Chandra:  acknowledge the Chandra Data Archive / CXC; cite ObsIDs (and the Chandra DOI for the dataset).
  XMM-Newton:  acknowledge the XMM-Newton Science Archive (ESA); cite ObsIDs.
  ESO:  "Based on observations collected at the European Southern Observatory under ESO programme(s) <ID>"  (IDs are in dbo.raw prog_id).
  ALMA:  "ADS/JAO.ALMA#<project code>"  (e.g. ADS/JAO.ALMA#2021.1.00675.S) plus the ALMA/ESO/NRAO/NAOJ line.
  Planck (PLA):  ESA/Planck Collaboration; cite the data-release paper for the map used.
  SIMBAD:  "This research has made use of the SIMBAD database, operated at CDS, Strasbourg, France"; cite Wenger et al. 2000 A&AS 143 9.
  VizieR / CDS TAP:  cite Ochsenbein, Bauer & Marcout 2000 A&AS 143 23.
  HEASARC:  "This research has made use of data obtained from the HEASARC, provided by NASA's Goddard Space Flight Center."
  OpenAlex (citation counts):  CC0; state the query date. Counts are from OpenAlex/INSPIRE and undercount vs ADS.
Standing protocol: every download of another person's work also goes to ContextPlease/claude/references/INDEX.md and ~/.clauderc_citations.

